119	}
120	```
121	
122	See [02 — Size limits](02-toon-format.md#size-limits) for why the caps exist and how they surface.
123	
124	### Serde Integration (`list()`)
125	
126	When the `serde` feature is enabled, `toon::list()` serializes any `T: serde::Serialize` slice to a rendered TOON string:
127	
128	```rust
129	#[cfg(feature = "serde")]
130	pub fn list<T: serde::Serialize>(
131	    type_name: impl Into<String>,
132	    items: &[T],
133	) -> Result<String, ToonError>;
134	```
135	
136	Items are serialized to JSON text and read back (so an `f32` field keeps its own shortest digits, `0.1` rather than `0.10000000149011612`) and must produce JSON objects (structs or maps). Non-object items and a reserved `type_name` (the same list `validate` rejects) return `Err(ToonError)`, and so does a key union wider than `MAX_FIELDS` or an `items.len() × fields` table larger than `MAX_CELLS` (checked before any row is built). A key missing from some items renders as `null` in those rows; nested arrays/objects become their compact JSON text, quoted.
137	
138	## Response Compositor (`error`, `response`, `idempotency`)
139	
140	### `DomainError`
141	
142	`DomainError` provides classified domain error responses (**AXI P6**):
