522	impl Pipeline {
523	    pub fn new(steps: Vec<PipelineStep>) -> Self;
524	    pub fn render(&self) -> String;                           // step[N]{id,name,status,reason}:, or step: []
525	}
526	
527	// michi_core::audience
528	#[non_exhaustive]
529	pub enum Audience { Assistant, User } // serde: "assistant" / "user"
530	
531	// michi_core::telemetry
532	#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default)]
533	pub struct NoopProvider;
534	impl NoopProvider {
535	    pub fn span(&self, name: &str);             // no-op
536	    pub fn count(&self, name: &str, value: u64); // no-op
537	}
538	```
539	
540	The structs above are `#[non_exhaustive]` from 0.4.0: build them with their constructors, then read or assign their public fields as before (`PartialSuccess` is read through its getters). Struct literals and exhaustive destructuring work only inside michi-core, so adding a field later is not a breaking change. `Value`, `KvValue`, `AlreadyDone`, `RetryConfigError` and the other enums marked `#[non_exhaustive]` above need a `_` arm in a `match` outside michi-core.
541	
542	`KvValue::Float(f, decimals)` rounds `f` to `decimals` places and writes the rounded value in canonical TOON number form, so `Float(1.5, 3)` is `1.5`, not `1.500`; `KvValue::FULL_PRECISION` (255) never rounds, so `Float(5e-324, KvValue::FULL_PRECISION)` is `5e-324` in TOON and in the JSON companions, while a smaller count rounds as asked (`Float(1e-300, 2)` is `0`); `Missing` is `null`; `Duration` is the string `1.5s`. `AgentResponse`'s KV path turns a `KvError` into a `kv_validation_failed` error body and sets `is_error`, like `toon_validation_failed` on the TOON path.
543	
544	## `truncate` — Char-Boundary Truncation
